package dev.cajeta.xgboost.objective;

/**
 * Which loss the booster minimizes — XGBoost's `objective` parameter.
 *
 *   SQUARED_ERROR  `reg:squarederror` — one output group, identity link
 *   LOGISTIC       `binary:logistic`  — one output group, sigmoid link
 *   SOFTMAX        `multi:softmax`    — K output groups, softmax link
 *
 * The objective decides three things and nothing else: the initial margin
 * ({@link SquaredError#baseMargin} and friends), the per-row gradient pair,
 * and the number of output groups grown per boosting round. Everything
 * downstream — the quantile sketch, the fixed-point histogram, the split
 * search, the tree layout — is objective-agnostic, which is why a K-class
 * model is just K trees per round over K gradient slices.
 */
public enum Objective {
    SQUARED_ERROR,
    LOGISTIC,
    SOFTMAX
}
